1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,721
This comparison uses the latest R zero three assembly as the baseline.

2
00:00:04,721 --> 00:00:09,091
The proposal keeps the same external gun envelope and target position.

3
00:00:09,091 --> 00:00:18,457
The changes are concentrated in the copper cooling body, copper backplate, steel return yoke, magnets, two water seals, and the upper coolant routing.

4
00:00:18,457 --> 00:00:21,017
This is a mechanical accommodation study.

5
00:00:21,017 --> 00:00:25,450
Balanced magnetic operation has not yet been simulated or demonstrated.

6
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:32,306
The original pack has twelve eight millimetre rods and two twelve millimetre centre discs.

7
00:00:32,306 --> 00:00:39,864
The proposal uses two six by ten millimetre discs at each outer position, and two twenty by ten millimetre discs at the centre.

8
00:00:39,864 --> 00:00:43,078
All are intended to be axially magnetized N forty two.

9
00:00:43,078 --> 00:00:45,637
The pack length remains twenty millimetres.

10
00:00:45,637 --> 00:00:49,089
The revised outer pitch circle is fifty eight millimetres.

11
00:00:49,089 --> 00:00:53,850
The pole area ratio is one point zero eight, which is only a screening estimate.

12
00:00:55,350 --> 00:01:00,615
Here the right hand view deliberately puts the larger centre magnet into the unmodified head.

13
00:01:00,615 --> 00:01:07,181
A twenty one millimetre clearance bore would leave only zero point five five millimetres to the old coolant channel.

14
00:01:07,181 --> 00:01:10,521
More decisively, it removes the original inner seal groove.

15
00:01:10,521 --> 00:01:14,484
The original coolant port counterbores also overlap the enlarged bore.

16
00:01:14,484 --> 00:01:18,050
So enlarging only the centre hole is not a workable conversion.

17
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:26,843
The revised copper cooling body moves the water annulus outward while keeping its five millimetre width and seven millimetre depth.

18
00:01:26,843 --> 00:01:30,462
The centre blind well becomes twenty one millimetres in diameter.

19
00:01:30,462 --> 00:01:35,639
The outer wells become six point four millimetres and move outward four millimetres radially.

20
00:01:35,639 --> 00:01:40,204
The external profile, target seat, and existing attachment patterns are preserved.

21
00:01:40,204 --> 00:01:46,050
The larger channel volume does not prove cooling performance; that still needs thermal and flow analysis.

22
00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:52,742
The backplate needs matching magnet holes, new seal grooves, and moved coolant connections.

23
00:01:52,742 --> 00:01:58,277
The nominal inner water seal changes to twenty three by two, and the outer to forty three by two.

24
00:01:58,277 --> 00:02:02,442
The port axes move four point four five millimetres outward on each side.

25
00:02:02,442 --> 00:02:07,748
The existing five millimetre through passages and fitting counterbore diameters are retained.

26
00:02:07,748 --> 00:02:16,250
The two millimetre seal section and nominal gland depth are retained, but these remain seal design candidates rather than a qualified sealing system.

27
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:22,364
Moving the coolant ports also moves the fitting clearance holes in the steel yoke.

28
00:02:22,364 --> 00:02:27,484
Its outside diameter, thickness, and attachment positions can stay unchanged in this study.

29
00:02:27,484 --> 00:02:32,604
The reference fitting envelopes move with the ports, and the upper hose bends are rerouted.

30
00:02:32,604 --> 00:02:36,767
The lower service tube and RF connection stay in their existing positions.

31
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:43,350
The actual purchased fittings, hose bend radius, yoke saturation, and electrical performance still need confirmation.

32
00:02:44,850 --> 00:02:51,533
The result is a local redesign of the magnetic and cooling head, rather than a redesign of the complete gun.

33
00:02:51,533 --> 00:03:05,208
The enlarged centre magnet can be accommodated inside the original external envelope, but it triggers coordinated changes to the water channel, both water seals, coolant ports, outer magnet locations, and yoke clearances.

34
00:03:05,208 --> 00:03:12,138
The target system, spacer, insulation, base, shields, mounting tube, and RF hardware are retained geometrically.

35
00:03:12,138 --> 00:03:17,150
The next engineering stage is magnetic and thermal validation before fabrication.
